From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 04:09:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 114/161] hjviewer: review fixes, cmui lane (1.9)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

TV-W2/TV-W6 connection window fit (major): the 1.8.2 card filled the
300 x 490 window to the pixel, so the caution box with a contact, P5 and
the recording line pushed [수락]/[거부] below the window on a PC without
HJViewer installed ([수락 및 권한 상승] shows). The card's column is now
hjv_cm_layout.dart's HjvCmCardColumn: the header on top, the buttons and
the notes above them whole at the bottom, and the permissions board
between them giving up height (its grid scrolls), with the recording line
whole under it. Letting the notes scroll instead would have squeezed the
caution to nothing where it matters. test/hjviewer_cm_fit_test.dart
measures the card at its real size with Pretendard, Korean and English,
elevate shown. cm_demo.dart opens at the real size.

TV-W6 P4 mark line (minor): two lines at most (English P4 needs about
205 px of 174), so the words S10 and P6 quote are never cut. The mark
line and the caution box's look moved to hjv_cm_layout.dart unchanged
otherwise, so the pure test measures the app's own widgets.

TV-W6 S13 (minor, security, critic S-08): S13 connects with one click, so
it now also says "도움받을 분에게 이 ID가 맞는지 확인하세요." /
"Check with the person you are helping that this is their ID."

TV-W6 S12/S13 (nit): "PC {ID}에서 지원 코드를 넣었습니다." instead of a
particle that depends on the ID's last digit.

TV-W6 hjv_account.rs (nit): the "no support proof" line is throttled
(one per minute); the peer decides how many Hash messages come.

TV-W6 support.rs (nit): a 200 to the code-making request of the current
login counts as fresh for S-02; the stored rev belongs to the login it
answered, and a new waiting thread's first request goes without one.

TV-W6 S-02 401 (nit): kept as an accepted deviation (no proof, no mark;
the login ends with the next account request's 401), recorded in the
docs note.

TV-W6 P6 (nit): the toast says P2's words when the core's pc-code result
says "staff": false; lane A's guest.rs follow-up writes that field.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
